    {
      "id": 161186,
      "name": "Foote",
      "username": "Foote",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-02-10T19:45:20.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Kingofsouls\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/k/58f4c7/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Kingofsouls:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>So, last night I was playing a game with Expatriette. She had a Speed Loading in play and a Ammo in hand. Speed Loading states that at the start of her turn, Expat can play 1 Ammo. The rules of the game state that if you do not play a card or use a power during your turn, you draw two cards during your draw step.</p>\n<p>My question is this: If I use Speed Loading to play my Ammo, but do not play a card during my play step, do I draw one or two cards? My guess is that I only draw one card since it Ammo was played instead of being put into play (even though it was outside my play step), but I am not sure if there is a hidden rule that I'm not seeing.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>The way I interpret the rule is you must skip your \"play phase\" and your \"power phase\". If you got to play a card during your SoT Phase, I don't think that counts.</p>",
