    {
      "id": 161193,
      "name": "dpt",
      "username": "dpt",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dpt/{size}/1922_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-02-10T20:24:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ronway\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/48/1856_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ronway:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>It can be tested. Have Omnitron-X have Slip Through Time in play while Fixed Point is in play, Skip the Play and Power phases , draw two cards, and see if you can play and use a power at the End of Turn phase.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Can someone confirm that they have tried this or something similar in the video game?</p>\n<p>I'm also curious about an effect that lets you play a card at the beginning of the turn, something like KNYFE's Overdo It (except that KNYFE isn't in the video game yet).</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>EDIT: Never mind, I found this explicitly mentioned in the <a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/clarifications-and-decisions-from-handelabra-christophers-fireside-chats-6773\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Fireside Chats</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<span>If you play a card via Speed Loading, then skip your play and power phases, you do not get to draw an extra card. The rule book says: \"If, for any reason, a player neither plays a card nor uses a power on their turn, then they may draw an additional card during their draw phase.\" \n</span></blockquote>",
      "post_number": 9,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:41:46.138Z",
