      "raw": "[quote=\"Ronway\"]\n It can be tested. Have Omnitron-X have Slip Through Time in play while Fixed Point is in play, Skip the Play and Power phases , draw two cards, and see if you can play and use a power at the End of Turn phase.  \n[/quote]\nCan someone confirm that they have tried this or something similar in the video game? \n\nI&#39;m also curious about an effect that lets you play a card at the beginning of the turn, something like KNYFE&#39;s Overdo It (except that KNYFE isn&#39;t in the video game yet).\n\n&nbsp;\n\nEDIT: Never mind, I found this explicitly mentioned in the <a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/clarifications-and-decisions-from-handelabra-christophers-fireside-chats-6773\">Fireside Chats</a>:\n<blockquote>\n<span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family: 'Open Sans', HelveticaNeue, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.4px; line-height: 21.6px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">If you play a card via Speed Loading, then skip your play and power phases, you do not get to draw an extra card. The rule book says: &quot;If, for any reason, a player neither plays a card nor uses a power on their turn, then they may draw an additional card during their draw phase.&quot; \n</blockquote>",
