      "raw": "<p>I remember there being some disagreement on what would happen when the Wager Master reverses the turn phases. Some people said that if you draw two in your Draw phase you&#39;re not allowed to use a power or play a card because you already drew two. Other people said that it wouldn&#39;t matter whether you drew two or note because the Draw phase only looks at whether you&#39;ve played a card or used a power <em>so far</em> on your turn, and as the Draw phase is now coming before either of those two phases it satisfies that rule and you can draw two and still do the other things.</p><p>I&#39;m still not sure which is correct, lol.</p>",
